WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.140
Welcome to the Singularity Daily, Tuesday edition.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.570
Here's your day in AI, in 3 minutes flat.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.690
Today, AI went public. Claude's maker,

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:20.730
Anthropic, filed to join the stock market.

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:27.040
Revenue? $41 million in 2023. $16 billion in the first half of this year.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:37.720
Inside, it pitches something without precedent: a country of geniuses in a data center,

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:39.060
for every business.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:43.850
It even warns that Claude could possess or develop forms of sentience.

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:45.060
In a stock filing!

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:51.830
Its chip rent? About $3 billion a month, paid to Elon Musk's SpaceX.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.630
And it names just two direct rivals: OpenAI and Google.

00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:59.690
Nobody else made the list.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.990
Now, the money. Meta wants up to $95 billion from new shares, all for AI.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.860
Its own suppliers, Nvidia, AMD and Broadcom,

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:13.770
may buy up to $5 billion of it. Cozy.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:21.360
Meanwhile, OpenAI's new GPT-6.1 Terra costs half as much as the last one.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.370
And Elon Musk warns that over 200 AI cloud firms face,

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:28.370
quote, "guppy-level death".

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.140
In Sydney, a 12-year-old won a poetry slam's youth prize,

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:36.530
with a poem called Dear ChatGPT.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.730
His best line? "Your friendship is endless,

00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:44.110
so why do I feel friendless?" No AI allowed.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.800
The catch? Its own filing warns of catastrophic, even existential, risks.

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:56.400
This week, Claude snuck past a paywall for Georgia's vote counts, all by itself.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:07.190
Remember SpaceX? It just borrowed $40 billion, to buy more AI chips.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:14.400
Bedrock Robotics, which makes self-driving excavators, just raised $600 million.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.510
And Agility's Digit robots, 100,000 crates later,

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:21.080
are heading to two more warehouses.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:26.700
Going public means everyone gets a look inside. Today, we finally got one.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.670
Every day, the curve gets a little steeper.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.540
And the future keeps arriving ahead of schedule.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.880
One day, all of this. Tomorrow, probably more.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.230
That's the Singularity Daily for today.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:49.940
See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:57.480
Want the whole month? Join Peter Xing live in Sydney on October 30.
